  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "120",
  "quote": "No landlord may increase the rent charged to a tenant, or to an assignee under section 95, during the term of their tenancy by more than the guideline",
  "reason": "The clause accurately reflects the statutory rules for rent increases under the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006, including the 12-month interval under section 119, the 90-day written notice requirement in an approved form under section 116, and the guideline cap under section 120. Because it is consistent with the Act, it is not made void by section 4."
}

